// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/call_h264_probe.t27 -- the H.264 video of a T27 OS call over the real socket, two processes on this
// machine (owner, 2026-10-23). Not the app and not the proof of the app: a headless driver of the cs_* API with the
// window's two codec blocks (call_vt vte_new / vtd_new) and synthetic camera frames instead of the camera. Each side
// makes 1280x720 BGRA frames on IOSurfaces at 30 a second (a grey level that changes and a moving bar), hands them to
// its encoder as the camera thread would, and takes the decoded pictures of the other side as the window would. The
// audio test pattern runs beside it, so the sound and the video share the sealed channel exactly as in a call.
//   CS_ROLE=caller|callee   (required) CS_PORT / CS_PEER_PORT (127.0.0.1; caller 47791, callee 47792)
//   CS_HSECS=20              seconds of video after the call is ACTIVE (the caller hangs up then)
// Each side prints HSTAT lines once a second (pictures decoded in that second, the session's numbers) and checks:
// both ends agreed on H.264, at least 28 pictures a second on average and 25 in the slowest 5 seconds, 1280x720,
// nothing lost, no decoder refusal (at most a second held back at the start), the sound kept flowing (at least 95 frames a second accepted).
// Build (Apple silicon):
//   t27b build specs/t27os/call_h264_probe.t27 -o chp.o --macho
//   ld -arch arm64 -platform_version macos 11.0 $(xcrun --show-sdk-version) -syslibroot $(xcrun --show-sdk-path) \
//      -e _main -lSystem -lffi -framework CoreFoundation -framework Security -framework AudioToolbox \
//      -framework CoreGraphics -framework ImageIO -framework CoreMedia -framework CoreVideo -framework VideoToolbox \
//      -framework IOSurface -o chp chp.o
// Test identities only (fixed fingerprints). Refs gHashTag/t27#11560.
module T27osCallH264Probe;

